&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for driving strategic sourcing initiatives, managing supplier relationships, and optimizing costs across various indirect categories, including Mapping, Customer Platforms, and Identity and Integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate complex contracts, deliver savings, manage stakeholder relationships, build category strategies, and implement sourcing best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives and strategy, leveraging technology and data analytics to enhance sourcing effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the end-to-end procurement process, including market analysis, RFx development, supplier evaluation, and contract negotiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Supply Chain Management, Business Administration, Engineering, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 years of experience in job offered, procurement, or related occupation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least three (3) years of experience with strategic technology sourcing, with a focus on indirect categories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least three (3) years of experience with procurement technology platforms, analytics tools, and Google Workspace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with analyzing and interpreting data, and making data-driven decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with project management, including leading multiple projects simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
