&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Machine Learning Engineer to join our Machine Learning Platform (MLP) team. Our MLP team builds and operates the platform that supports online and offline ML model development, training, execution, and observability across Lyft. This role focuses on improving the quality and performance of ML models across the company, through: direct modeling work with partner teams, enhanced platform capabilities, and agentic ML systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and deliver ML platform features with well-defined scope, from technical specification to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with ML Engineers and Data Scientists across Lyft to identify and deliver improvements to production models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose model performance issues and apply improvements in feature engineering, model selection, training, and evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build platform capabilities that make it easier for teams to develop, evaluate, and improve their models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build agentic systems that automate parts of the model development lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate tradeoffs between model accuracy, system complexity, and runtime performance, including when a non-ML solution is more appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply statistical methods to model evaluation and experiment design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write tested, readable, and maintainable code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in code reviews, design reviews, on-call rotations, and incident response&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor deployed code and models for stability and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Estimate effort for assigned work and contribute to roadmap discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s or Master’s Degree in Computer Science, Statistics, Mathematics, or another quantitative STEM field, and relevant work experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of engineering experience (or 2+ with Master’s) building production systems in Python, Go, Java, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience building machine learning models and deploying them to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foundation in statistics, classical ML methods, experimentation, and model evaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ML frameworks (e.g. PyTorch, TensorFlow) and ML training, serving, and deployment infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to Have: Experience with GenAI and agentic systems, including AI assisted coding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended health and dental coverage options, along with life insurance and disability benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a Lyft funded Health Care Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RRSP plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
