&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is changing fast. We’re integrating acquired businesses, growing in Europe and new global markets, launching new lines of business, and building a workforce for autonomous vehicles alongside our corporate teams. Half of our team members now live outside the US. Our People team has to keep pace, and that means designing programs that work for a bigger, more global and more varied Lyft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The People Strategy &amp;amp; Programs team leads complex, cross-functional work that comes to the People organization. We run the People team’s operating rhythms and make sure our biggest priorities get delivered across every People vertical: HR Operations, Total Rewards, Talent Acquisition, Team Member Experience and People Business Partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As People Project Manager, you’ll own the operating rhythm and budget of the People team, including annual planning, OKRs and quarterly business reviews. You’ll also own workstreams within larger People programs, such as change management for a major cross-functional project or business initiative with large people impacts. You’ll report to the Chief of Staff to the Chief People Officer and work closely with People leaders and partners across the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for a problem solver who can run independently, build strong deliverables and keep work moving. You’ll coordinate across teams, develop materials leaders rely on, and track progress so nothing falls through the cracks. Over time, you’ll take on more facilitation and cross-functional work. Success looks like People team rhythms that run smoothly, workstreams that deliver on time, and leaders who trust your materials and updates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll work on:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the People team’s operating rhythm, including annual planning, OKR setting and tracking, quarterly business reviews and People leadership team meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the People team budget, including tracking spend, forecasting and partnering with Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own workstreams within larger People programs, such as change management for a major cross-functional project or business initiative with large people impacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Step into cross-functional gray areas where roles and responsibilities get blurry, and helping teams define ownership quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;By month 3: Running core People team rhythms independently, including OKR tracking, budget tracking and quarterly business review preparation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;By month 6: Owning 2 - 3 workstreams within cross-functional projects, with clear plans and regular status reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;By month 12: Leading the full annual planning and budget cycle for the People team and recognized as a reliable partner for coordination and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the planning and execution of People team rhythms, from calendars and pre-reads to follow-ups and action tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with People leaders to set OKRs, track progress and flag risks before they become problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing the People team budget, tracking spend against plan and flagging variances early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing workstream plans, milestones and status updates within larger programs, and escalating blockers with clear options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing high-quality materials, including decks, briefing documents, trackers and status reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting change management, including stakeholder mapping, readiness assessments, readiness checklists and manager materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clarifying roles and responsibilities when work crosses teams, and driving quick decisions on who owns what&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Using AI, automation and our People systems to streamline work, speed up reporting and help leaders make faster, better-informed decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing intake and prioritization so the People team works on the right things in the right order&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building templates, trackers and processes that make the team’s work more consistent and easier to run&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitating working sessions and meetings, building toward leading larger discussions with senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Defining success metrics for your projects and using data to report on progress and recommend adjustments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handling sensitive and confidential information with discretion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
