&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a quick study, who is no stranger to working with shifting rules and regulations, to join our team. You’ll operationalize business and regulatory requirements, advocate for process improvements, and collaborate with Legal, Product and Engineering to solve problems with solutions that scale across platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will balance growth objectives with regulatory requirements, but that won’t phase you as you’re no stranger to challenge or ambiguity. You have a deep sense of empathy for our users (both internally and externally) and excel in asking probing questions, detecting unstated assumptions, driving consensus, resolving conflicts, and prioritizing competing objectives. You enjoy learning new things and working with many people to achieve success. You consistently own the work, focus on delivering impact, and reimagine what’s possible. In short, you make it happen, and you do it with a great sense of humor and an excitement to change the face of ridesharing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Product and Engineering to develop new product solutions that improve our users’ experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategically plan and execute new process rollouts, operational workflows, and create comprehensive products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve internal processes to respond quickly and effectively to business needs and shifting regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross functionally to manage platform operations to improve our users’ experience and adjust to regulatory requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct analyses of the business impacts posed by regulatory requirements and proposed changes to Lyft’s operations and product offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop creative solutions and plans, with stakeholder visibility and buy-in, to operationalize business and regulatory changes in a market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on defining key success metrics and maintaining a working dashboard&amp;nbsp; to monitor performance for ongoing programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully handle shifting priorities and emerging situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of Operations experience, preferably with a Compliance/Regulatory background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Operations, Product, User Experience, Compliance, and/or Engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior detail orientation and organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success balancing multiple projects, deadlines, and requests&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience asking the right questions and reducing friction when working with diverse, cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly-developed written, verbal, and presentation communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter attitude with the ability to take initiative to set and achieve goals and deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated critical thinking and problem solving ability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using AI tools, such as LLM assistants like Claude, to speed up everyday work&lt;/li&gt;
