&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft&#39;s Healthcare &amp;amp; Community Access team is changing how cities, transit agencies, and state Medicaid agencies think about paratransit, microtransit, and non-emergency medical transportation (NEMT). We already partner with some of the largest transit agencies and NEMT brokers in the country to expand access to transit and healthcare, and shape a future where cities are built around people – not cars.&amp;nbsp; Now we&#39;re going after the rest of the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced sales and business development professional with a track record of unlocking new opportunities and a drive to keep raising the bar. This person will be responsible for net new business for our Transit and Healthcare verticals, building pipeline, designing the go-to-market strategy in partnership with our Lyft Business Strategy team, structuring creative deals, and driving them all the way to signature. You won&#39;t manage a book of existing accounts. Your job is to find, open, and win new ones, then hand them off to our Account Management team to grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for someone who is energized by a blank whiteboard and a long sales cycle, who treats an RFP loss as intel for the next bid, and who doesn&#39;t stop until the contract is signed. You&#39;ll work with a high degree of autonomy, bring energy and urgency that fuels the team, and&amp;nbsp; directly shape how we work with transit and healthcare partners on some of the most pressing mobility challenges facing communities today..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own net new revenue for the Transit and Healthcare verticals (weighted toward Transit), contributing to a team quota&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Lyft Business Strategy team to design the go-to-market strategy for Transit use cases, including paratransit, microtransit, first/last mile, and NEMT, then own execution end to end: targeting, messaging, outreach, qualification, and close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work an established target list and expand pipeline beyond it through prospecting, industry relationships, conferences, and creative outbound campaigns built with Marketing and Sales Ops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead public sector sales motions end to end, including tracking procurement cycles, influencing RFP requirements early, and working through RFP and RFI responses with cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structure creative, mutually beneficial deals, including new pricing and rebate models, pilots, and multi-party agreements, using cost/benefit analysis and unit economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive complex contract negotiations to completion with partner executives and procurement teams, working with Legal, Finance, Compliance, and Public Policy (on Lyft or client paper)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Lyft Business Strategy to build business cases for new segments, products, and service levels, sizing the opportunity and resource needs and making a clear go/no-go recommendation to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the voice of the market to Product, Engineering, and Product Marketing, identifying product gaps that block deals and championing the features that unlock new segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Lyft externally at transit, healthcare, and NEMT industry events, conferences, and panels, building Lyft&#39;s reputation and your own network in the space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hand off closed partnerships to Account Management with a clear plan for launch and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present pipeline, strategy, and results to VP-level and above audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of policy, government affairs, sales, or business development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years focused on net new enterprise or public sector business and a consistent record of exceeding quota is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building government affairs, public advocacy, sales and/or GTM strategies from scratch and executing them to close revenue and/or achieve policy outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to transit agencies, municipalities, state agencies, or healthcare organizations, including navigating public procurement and responding to RFPs; or direct experience working for an agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with complex and emerging technology architecture like APIs and MCPs preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of closing complex, long-cycle deals with multiple stakeholders and decision makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative deal structuring and strong negotiation skills, including comfort with financial modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persistence and resilience: you see “no” as “not yet” and keep finding new angles until you win&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly self-directed and comfortable with ambiguity; you set your own priorities, build your own pipeline, and go after high-impact opportunities without being asked&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and presentation skills, with the executive presence to pitch C-suite and agency leadership and adapt your message to each stakeholder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence cross-functional partners and build consensus inside and outside Lyft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transit, paratransit, microtransit, NEMT, or mobility industry experience strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
