&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Data Scientist, Decisions – Autonomous Vehicles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The future of Lyft is a hybrid network, where autonomous vehicles and human drivers serve riders side by side on one platform. That future has already started. In September 2026, Lyft riders in Nashville were matched with Waymo autonomous vehicles on the Lyft app for the first time. Our partnerships now span Waymo in Nashville, May Mobility in Atlanta and Baidu in Europe, with more on the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Growth organization is charting the future of Lyft’s growth beyond North American rideshare’s core products, including bringing Autonomous Vehicles (AVs) to riders domestically and abroad. As a Senior Data Scientist, Decisions for AV, you will be the science partner for the AV product team. You’ll use experimentation and data to decide what we build, how we launch it, and how we know it’s working. You will work closely with product managers, engineers, designers, operations and partnership leaders, and present your recommendations to senior leadership and AV partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will help us answer questions such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rider adoption and trust:&lt;/strong&gt; What makes a rider choose, accept or opt out of an autonomous ride, and which product changes increase adoption?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The AV product experience:&lt;/strong&gt; How should we design and test the experience from request to pickup to post-ride, including flows like airport pickups?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Launch decisions:&lt;/strong&gt; Which features are ready to scale, and how do we measure their impact before and after launch?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product health:&lt;/strong&gt; What metrics define a great AV experience for riders, and how do we monitor them across partners and markets?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership performance:&lt;/strong&gt; What shared product metrics and quality guardrails should define success with each AV partner?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help design, run and analyze A/B tests and other online experiments on AV products, and turn results into clear launch decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define the metrics framework for AV product success, including adoption, retention, trust and rider experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product managers, engineers and designers to identify opportunities and shape the AV product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build dashboards and analytical frameworks to monitor AV product and business performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present data-driven recommendations to senior leadership and AV partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with central science teams on experimentation best practices for a hybrid network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor data scientists and analysts across Global Growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Statistics, Economics, Mathematics, or a related quantitative field, or equivalent work experience; advanced degree preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in product data science or analytics, with a track record of work that changed product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep hands-on experience designing and analyzing online experiments at scale, including metric selection, power analysis and interpreting results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL on large datasets, and Python or R for analysis and visualization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting to senior stakeholders and influencing product decisions without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: experience in AVs, mobility, rideshare, delivery or other two-sided marketplaces; experimentation in marketplace settings; working with partner or third-party data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to turn ambiguous product questions into clear analyses and recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to choose the right experiment design for the decision, and explain the trade-off between rigor and speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to craft a compelling story with data for technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and real curiosity about how riders experience a new technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial self-starter who takes ownership in a fast-moving, ambiguous environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please submit your resume in English.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft may use artificial intelligence to screen applicants; however, Lyft employees make the ultimate selection and hiring decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job fills an existing vacancy.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every ride on Lyft runs on infrastructure. Every match between a rider and a driver, every price, every payment, every map and every arrival estimate depends on platforms that have to be fast, reliable and efficient at a global scale. This role leads the organization that builds and runs those platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Why this role matters&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is one of the most impactful engineering leadership roles at Lyft. You will be accountable for one of Lyft&#39;s largest operating investments: the cost of hosting, running and scaling the entire company on a public cloud, including our growing AI infrastructure spend. This role spans the full infrastructure stack, carries one of Lyft’s largest operating budgets, and directly determines how well Lyft’s product works and what it costs to run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to Lyft’s Chief Technology Officer, you will lead an organization of approximately 200 engineers, engineering managers and senior technical leaders to efficiently execute on the right goals to drive impact while maintaining a sense of community.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead the organization that builds and runs the platforms every Lyft engineer depends on. You’ll guide a team of engineering managers and senior technical leaders, and you’ll be accountable for the reliability, scalability and cost-efficiency of the systems that keep riders and drivers moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;What you’ll own&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core hosting infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;. The hosting and compute foundation Lyft runs on in the public cloud, including our Kubernetes clusters and container platform, networking, storage, and the core services every product team depends on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data infrastructure.&lt;/strong&gt; The databases, data stores and foundational data services that keep rider, driver and marketplace data available, durable and fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer platform and experience.&lt;/strong&gt; The internal platforms, tools, libraries, software development kits (SDKs), and build and release systems that determine how quickly and safely every Lyft engineer can ship.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobile and client infrastructure.&lt;/strong&gt; The shared build, release, testing and client platforms behind Lyft’s Android, iOS and web applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI and machine learning infrastructure.&lt;/strong&gt; The compute, serving and platform capabilities that let Lyft’s teams train, deploy and run machine learning and AI workloads, including the&amp;nbsp; capacity, reliability and cost discipline that AI product development requires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Observability and reliability.&lt;/strong&gt; Stats, logging, metrics and tracing across Lyft. You’ll also define and champion engineering-wide standards for reliability and operational excellence, and build the mechanisms that make them stick: service level objectives (SLOs), error budgets, incident review and production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure economics.&lt;/strong&gt; A significant operating budget across hosting, cloud and AI spend, including capacity planning, efficiency, unit economics, and the tradeoffs between cost, reliability and speed. You’ll drive sustained efficiency without compromising reliability, and make the cost of scale visible and understandable to the teams that create it, in close partnership with Finance and executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;How you’ll lead&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set strategy and plan.&lt;/strong&gt; Turn company priorities into a multi-year infrastructure strategy and roadmap, and own org-level planning, including headcount and budget, to put resources against the highest-leverage problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive major platform evolutions.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead cross-functional initiatives and platform changes, and make sure architectural decisions scale with Lyft’s growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Balancing speed and safety with continuous improvement.&lt;/strong&gt; Shape a culture where Lyft ships quickly without compromising production stability. Make the hard calls when the two are in tension, and instill continuous improvement in architecture, process and operational practices across your teams and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Represent infrastructure to executive leadership.&lt;/strong&gt; Communicate risks, tradeoffs and investment needs in business terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and develop the organization.&lt;/strong&gt; Hire, grow and retain strong engineering managers and senior technical leaders, building a deep bench and an inclusive, accountable organization with clear ownership and a high bar for performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;15+ years of progressive experience, including at least 5 years leading teams.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong technical background.&lt;/strong&gt; You contribute to planning and design discussions and earn the respect of senior engineers on consequential architecture decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Large-scale public cloud infrastructure.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve led infrastructure for a product that couldn’t afford to be down, including Kubernetes and container platforms, distributed systems, networking and storage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep experience in several of the following:&lt;/strong&gt; data infrastructure (databases, data stores, foundational data services); developer platforms and experience; mobile and client infrastructure for Android, iOS and web; and/or infrastructure for machine learning and AI workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understanding of Infrastructure economics at scale.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve owned a large cloud, hosting or infrastructure budget, delivered efficiency and cost outcomes without sacrificing reliability, and can speak fluently in business terms to the tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership at scale.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve led managers of managers and senior technical leaders in a large organization at comparable scale, and guided teams through planning, prioritization, execution and major platform migrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you work.&lt;/strong&gt; You focus on impact, execution and internal/external customers. You build teams and products that scale, collaborate well, instill a strong sense of ownership, and plan ahead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
