&lt;p&gt;Lyft’s Accounting team is looking for an experienced Senior Payroll Accountant to join us in Seattle. You’ll own core payroll accounting and month-end close work across our US and North American entities, keeping everything accurate, on time, and well controlled.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work closely with our Payroll, FP&amp;amp;A, and broader Accounting teams, and we’ll count on you to take ownership of your close tasks and help make our processes better over time. If you enjoy a clean reconciliation and a smooth close, we’d love to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own payroll-related journal entries for our US (HQ) and North American international subsidiaries, from preparation through booking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare payroll accruals, including monthly payroll, bonus, workers’ compensation, PTO, and commissions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete month-end and quarter-end close activities on schedule, in line with our internal close calendar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile and analyze payroll-related GL accounts in accordance with GAAP and Lyft’s accounting policies, and perform flux analysis to explain monthly and quarterly movements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve reconciling items in partnership with FP&amp;amp;A and the Payroll team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a deep understanding of our pay classes, pay codes, and payroll processing activities so you can connect what happens in payroll to what lands in the GL.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep payroll records organized and audit-ready, and help maintain and strengthen our internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to streamline or automate recurring close work, and help bring them to life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad hoc projects as they come up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting or Finance; CPA is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of general ledger accounting experience, including 2+ years in payroll accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience owning month-end close in a fast-paced, multi-entity environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of GAAP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work independently, stay organized, and hit deadlines without sacrificing accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, friendly communication and a collaborative approach with cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep respect for confidentiality and data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel skills (lookups, pivot tables, and clean, reviewable workpapers).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with finance and payroll systems such as Workday, Oracle, ADP Globalview, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a public company and familiarity with SOX controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting a payroll system implementation or process improvement project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
