&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is changing fast. We’re integrating acquired businesses, growing in Europe and new global markets, launching new lines of business, and building a workforce for autonomous vehicles alongside our corporate teams. Half of our team members now live outside the US. Our People team has to keep pace, and that means designing programs that work for a bigger, more global and more varied Lyft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The People Strategy &amp;amp; Programs team leads complex, cross-functional work that comes to the People organization. We run the People team’s operating rhythms and make sure our biggest priorities get delivered across every People vertical: HR Operations, Total Rewards, Talent Acquisition, Team Member Experience and People Business Partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior People Project Manager, you’ll own high-complexity programs end to end as the People team transforms alongside the business. You’ll report to the Chief of Staff to the Chief People Officer and partner closely with People leaders, Finance, Legal and business leaders across Lyft. This isn’t a role where you hand work off once the plan is set. You’ll facilitate the strategy, validate it with subject matter experts, lead when the work needs a leader, and get into the details to keep it moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for a systems thinker who’s comfortable with ambiguity and enjoys every part of the People function. Success looks like complex programs that land well, People leaders who see you as a trusted partner, and repeatable approaches that make the next big project easier than the last.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll work on:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; Your portfolio will shift with the business, but example programs include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standing up People programs for new and growing workforces, such as hourly and field teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with the business on workforce and location strategy: the right roles in the right places at the right cost&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving AI and automation adoption across the People team, from prioritization through measuring impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing org structures and ways of working built for speed and scale, from spans and layers to decision rights and our matrix model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;By month 3: Owning 1 - 3 active programs with clear plans, owners, metrics and status reporting in place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;By month 6: Leading at least one major cross-functional program, such as an integration or org design effort, with minimal oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;By month 12: Recognized by People leaders as the go-to partner for complex, cross-functional work, with at least one repeatable playbook or framework in use across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning complex, cross-functional People programs from scoping through delivery, defining strategy, milestones and success metrics, and adapting plans as business needs change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turning ambiguous problems into clear, actionable plans, and working through options independently before escalating&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitating strategy discussions with People and business leaders, and validating recommendations with subject matter experts across the People team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building strong relationships with senior leaders and assembling the right cross-functional teams to deliver&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing executive-ready deliverables, including decks, recommendations, decision documents and change communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading change management for org changes, integrations and new programs, including stakeholder management, change readiness assessments, manager preparation and coordination with internal communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesizing data across programs to weigh short-term trade-offs against long-term goals and influence scope and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating scalable program plans, templates and project management standards so People teams run work the same way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Getting into the details when needed to remove blockers and keep work moving&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handling sensitive and confidential information with discretion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience across program management, HR business partnering, HR generalist work, management consulting or business operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HR business partner, People business partner or HR generalist experience strongly preferred, with a broad understanding of how People functions work together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consulting experience preferred, especially in organizational design, change management or transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record owning complex, cross-functional programs end to end in ambiguous environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing senior leaders and building alignment across teams with competing priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and systems thinking, with the ability to see how decisions in one area affect others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication and experience creating executive-level materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using data to measure progress and support recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with M&amp;amp;A integration, restructuring or global expansion preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools to improve how work gets done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
