&lt;p&gt;The Central TPM team drives Lyft’s highest-impact product and technology initiatives from concept to launch. Central TPMs are technically strong program leaders who operate from a product and engineering point of view and bridge the gap to other functions, such as comms, marketing, BD, support, and external partners, ensuring each is a core partner in the program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They are both strategic and tactical, and they do what it takes to deliver top-priority programs that have a material impact on the business, from new product launches to acquisitions and strategic partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-own program strategy with Product and Engineering, and influence company strategy, technical architecture, and roadmap tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end delivery of Lyft’s top-priority cross-functional initiatives from concept to launch, with clear goals, milestones, and definition of done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute integration roadmaps, strategies, and playbooks for acquisitions and strategic partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how the program runs, including roles and decision rights, escalation paths, and communication plan, and hold workstream owners accountable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate risks early, drive mitigation plans, and aggressively resolve systemic issues blocking delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate with transparency at every level, from engineers to the C-suite, sharing progress, risks, and tradeoffs clearly and directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present data-backed options to decision makers and drive decisions to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to team health by building delivery best practices, mentoring other TPMs, and supporting recruiting and onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in Technical Program Management or a TPM/PM hybrid role, including leading large, highly cross-functional programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background in software engineering, systems engineering, or data science, strong enough to go deep with engineers and product leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering programs on large-scale production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to operate autonomously in significant ambiguity, with only high-level direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of shaping strategy and roadmaps, with strong dependency and risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence, negotiate, and build alignment in a matrixed environment without formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience bridging product and engineering with business functions, such as in acquisitions, partnerships, or go-to-market launches, is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended health and dental coverage options, along with life insurance and disability benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to a Lyft funded Health Care Savings Account&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;RRSP plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
