&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;L&#39;échelle salariale de base prévue pour ce poste dans la région de Longueuil est de 34 $ à 36 $/heure CAD. Les échelles salariales varient en fonction de divers facteurs, notamment les qualifications, l&#39;expérience et la situation géographique. Votre recruteur pourra vous fournir davantage de précisions sur l&#39;échelle salariale propre à votre lieu de travail et sur les autres facteurs pris en compte durant le processus d&#39;embauche.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lyft is becoming a global hybrid transportation platform. More people than ever are making Lyft part of their everyday lives, and we&#39;re building on a strong foundation to get there. That work spans Europe through Freenow and our expanded presence in London, autonomous vehicle operations through Flexdrive, and a growing network of partnerships. As our CEO has said, &quot;the opportunity ahead is massive, and we&#39;re just getting started.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our senior-most communications leader, you&#39;ll own how that story is told to every audience: riders, drivers, employees, investors, policymakers, partners, and the media. Reporting directly to the CEO and serving on the executive leadership team, you&#39;ll lead a seasoned organization spanning Corporate, Product, Consumer, Brand Communications, Policy Communications, Content, and Social, with teams in the U.S. and Europe and full ownership of the function’s budget and resources. You&#39;ll set the enterprise narrative, guide the company through the moments that matter most, and act as a trusted counselor to the CEO, the executive team, and the board.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and steward Lyft&#39;s corporate, consumer, and technology narratives so every launch, partnership, and milestone ladders up to a clear and differentiated story&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic advisor to the CEO and executive team on reputation, positioning, and stakeholder impact, and shape the CEO&#39;s external voice across media, industry stages, and investor forums&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate emerging reputation risks and lead the company through complex, high-visibility issues with speed, clarity, and sound judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build deep, trusted relationships with top-tier journalists, editors, and influencers to shape how the market understands Lyft&#39;s vision, progress, and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Marketing and Product to bring new products, services, and partnerships to market through integrated campaigns that drive awareness and preference&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Investor Relations, Policy, and Legal to keep financial, regulatory, and public narratives aligned, including partnership on the company’s disclosure process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape Lyft’s policy and social impact narrative in partnership with Policy teams, supporting the company’s positions with regulators, legislators, and community stakeholders across our markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build owned content and storytelling programs, including human-interest storytelling and answer-engine (AI) discoverability, so Lyft’s story is discoverable where people search&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and retain a senior, high-performing communications organization, setting a high bar for craft and a culture of learning from both wins and misses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the communications budget and headcount, allocating resources against the company’s highest-priority narratives and moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the metrics that matter for reputation and communications impact, and use them to guide investment and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion the adoption of AI across the communications function, including AI-powered media monitoring, sentiment analysis, and content development, to increase speed, insight, and scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive senior communications leadership spanning corporate and consumer, including experience leading the function or serving as the top communications advisor to a CEO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a global team and owning a function-level budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record at technology or tech-enabled consumer companies operating in competitive, high-scrutiny industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with consumer brands where sentiment shifts quickly, with a strong read on cultural, social, and public trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with policy or regulatory communications in a highly regulated or politically scrutinized industry strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build narratives that align with company strategy and move audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven judgment leading through crises and high-stakes issues in the public eye&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, durable relationships with top-tier media, editors, and influencers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public company experience, including partnership with Investor Relations on earnings and investor communications, strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of building and retaining high-performing teams and developing future communications leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of evaluating and adopting AI-driven capabilities within a communications organization, such as tools for monitoring, insight, and content workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great medical, dental, and vision insurance options with additional programs available when enrolled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family building benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Child care and pet benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) plan with company match to help save for your future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In addition to 12 observed holidays, salaried team members have discretionary paid time off, hourly team members have 15 days paid time off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18 weeks of paid parental leave. Biological, adoptive, and foster parents are all eligible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized commuter benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly Lyft credits and complimentary Lyft Pink membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft is an equal opportunity employer committed to an inclusive workplace that fosters belonging. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regards to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, age, genetic information, or any other basis prohibited by law. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Lyft highly values having employees working in-office to foster a collaborative work environment and company culture. This role will be in-office on a hybrid schedule — Team Members will be expected to work in the office 3 days per week on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Thursdays. Lyft considers working in the office at least 3 days per week to be an essential function of this hybrid role. Your recruiter can share more information about the various in-office perks Lyft offers. Additionally, hybrid roles have the flexibility to work from anywhere for up to 4 weeks per year. #Hybrid&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The expected base pay range for this position in San Francisco is $325,000 - $375,000. In addition to the base pay, this role is eligible for competitive equity awards, bonuses, and benefits. You can read more about Lyft’s employee benefits &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.lyft.com/careers/life-at-lyft&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Total compensation is dependent on a variety of factors, including qualifications, experience, and geographic location. Your recruiter can share more information about the salary range specific to your working location and other factors during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At Lyft, our purpose is to serve and connect. We aim to achieve this by cultivating a work environment where all team members belong and have the opportunity to thrive.&amp;nbsp; Flexdrive is a subsidiary of Lyft that works together with Lyft teams to realize our shared mission.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flexdrive builds the operational backbone for the future of mobility. As a leader in fleet management and a Lyft subsidiary, we&#39;re extending our expertise into autonomous vehicle (AV) infrastructure: managing the physical operations that keep AV fleets safe, available, and performing at scale. Our Nashville depot is the first proof point in a multi-market expansion, and we&#39;re building the team to sustain and scale it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Program Manager, AV Technical Services, Flexdrive is seeking a Training Lead to own technical training and qualification for the team who service and repair our autonomous vehicle fleet. These are electric, sensor-equipped vehicles that run around the clock, so every repair, inspection, and return-to-service decision has to be done right the first time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll train and certify Flexdrive associates to our AV partner&#39;s standards, keep them qualified, and use quality data to find and close skill gaps on the shop floor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Training Program Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run day-to-day technical training and qualification for Flexdrive team members, executing the training plan set by AV Technical Services leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete the AV partner&#39;s Train-the-Trainer certification, then serve as Lead Instructor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver training per partner requirements: web-based modules, hands-on demonstrations, OJT checklists, and practical skills assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain curriculum, SOP-based job aids, and quick-reference guides covering:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;high-voltage safety, de-energization, and lockout/tagout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;preventive maintenance and multi-point inspections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;tires, brakes, suspension, and steering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;sensor inspection, cleaning, replacement, and calibration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;diagnostics, scan tools, and partner-directed software procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;torque specs, critical fasteners, and quality checks before return to service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;accurate repair documentation in work orders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain all training records in the partner LMS. Run monthly verification reviews so the team stays 100% current and audit-ready.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sure no Flexdrive associate performs a task without an active qualification. Manage expirations, recertifications, and remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and report time-to-qualify, first-attempt pass rate, and qualification coverage by shift and task.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Performance &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use quality data to find skill gaps and deliver targeted retraining. Relevant signals include:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;rework and comebacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;failed quality checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;repeat repairs on the same vehicle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;safety incidents and near misses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;audit findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAPAs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend regular time on the shop floor across shifts, demonstrating repairs, observing associates and technicians, and coaching in the moment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep your own hands-on skills current, and step in on complex repairs as needed to model the standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Roll out training for new procedures, vehicle platforms, hardware, and software changes on partner timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support root cause investigations where training is a contributing factor, and update materials to close the gap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flag unclear or missing repair procedures to the AV partner and push for updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align with service partner leads, Repair Coordinators, and fleet operations so the whole depot works from the same process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Recruiting on technician skills benchmarks and hands-on hiring assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a culture of safety, including high-voltage PPE, lift safety, and safe vehicle movement, working closely with EHS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a repeatable technical training playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Schedule &amp;amp; Travel&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based at our Nashville depot, with flexibility to cover day and overnight shifts for training and observations. Some weekends as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 25-50% to support training at other Flexdrive and partner sites. Travel volume varies with business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on the shop floor for extended periods, including standing, bending, kneeling, and working under vehicles on lifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lift and carry up to 50 lbs.&lt;/li&gt;
